>Answer key: reviewed in class.</div></div><div class="task"><span class="practice-badge">Precision</span><h3>Activity E — Turn Data into Academic Sentences</h3><p>Use each data card to replace the vague statement with one precise sentence.</p><div class="data-card"><strong>Battery test:</strong> 4.2 V initial · 3.0 V cut-off · 200 mA load · 8.6 h operation</div><div class="prompt">The battery lasted a long time.</div><textarea placeholder="Rewrite using the data..."></textarea><div class="data-card"><strong>Controller test:</strong> THD 7.8% → 2.4% · load = 1.5 kW</div><div class="prompt">The controller gave much better results.</div><textarea placeholder="Rewrite using the data..."></textarea><div class="data-card"><strong>Motor test:</strong> stator temperature 42 °C → 76 °C · 25 min · rated load</div><div class="prompt">The motor became hot.</div><textarea placeholder="Rewrite using the data..."></textarea><div class="student-answer-note">Answer key: reviewed in class.</div></div><div class="task"><span class="practice-badge">Hedging</span><h3>Activity F — Choose the Right Strength of Claim</h3><p>Select the sentence that best matches the evidence described.</p><div class="choice-row"><strong>1. One laboratory test produced a lower ripple value.</strong><label><input name="h1" type="radio"/> The test proves that the method eliminates ripple.</label><label><input name="h1" type="radio"/> The result suggests that the method may reduce ripple under the tested condition.</label></div><div class="choice-row"><strong>2. Three repeated measurements showed a similar trend.</strong><label><input name="h2" type="radio"/> The measurements indicate that the output tends to stabilise after 5 s.</label><label><input name="h2" type="radio"/> The measurements prove that the output always stabilises after 5 s.</label></div><div class="choice-row"><strong>3. The simulation alone shows lower current distortion.</strong><label><input name="h3" type="radio"/> The simulation results suggest a reduction in current distortion.</label><label><input name="h3" type="radio"/> The proposed system definitely removes current distortion in all operating conditions.</label></div><div class="choice-row"><strong>4. A measured value is close to, but not exactly, 100 V.</strong><label><input name="h4" type="radio"/> The measured voltage was approximately 100 V.</label><label><input name="h4" type="radio"/> The measured voltage was exactly 100 V.</label></div><div class="student-answer-note">Answer key: reviewed in class.</div></div><div class="task"><span class="practice-badge">Error clinic</span><h3>Activity G — Correct the Sentence</h3><p>Correct the Academic English problem in each sentence.</p><ol><li>The equipments were tested before the experiment.<input placeholder="Correct sentence" type="text"/></li><li>We discussed about the voltage drop in the report.<input placeholder="Correct sentence" type="text"/></li><li>The voltage dropped, the controller restarted.<input placeholder="Correct sentence" type="text"/></li><li>Figure 2 showed the measured current waveform.<input placeholder="Correct sentence" type="text"/></li><li>An induction three phase motor was used.<input placeholder="Correct sentence" type="text"/></li><li>The researches show many informations about the converter.<input placeholder="Correct sentence" type="text"/></li></ol><div class="student-answer-note">Answer key: reviewed in class.</div></div><div class="task"><span class="practice-badge">Editing</span><h3>Activity H — Repair a Short Technical Paragraph</h3><p>Rewrite the paragraph so it is more formal, precise and objective. Correct the sentence-level problems as well.</p><div class="editing-passage">We looked at the inverter and it worked really good. The output was very stable, the voltage changed only a little. We used some equipment to check it. The new controller is amazing and it proves that our design is the best. The test was done for a while and the temperature got high.</div><textarea placeholder="Write your improved paragraph here..." style="min-height:180px"></textarea><div class="student-answer-note">Answer key: reviewed in class.</div></div><div class="task"><span class="practice-badge">Fast finisher</span><h3>Activity I — 5-Minute Academic Upgrade</h3><p>Improve all four sentences. Aim for one clear improvement in each: register, precision, objectivity or technical vocabulary.</p><div class="prompt">1. The current went up a lot.</div><input placeholder="Improved sentence" type="text"/><div class="prompt">2. We got good results from the filter.</div><input placeholder="Improved sentence" type="text"/><div class="prompt">3. The software is really easy and works perfectly.</div><input placeholder="Improved sentence" type="text"/><div class="prompt">4. The motor made a big noise.</div><input placeholder="Improved sentence" type="text"/><div class="student-answer-note">Answer key: reviewed in class.</div></div></div></section><section id="diagnostic"><div class="head"><div><span class="label">83–98 minutes</span><h2>Diagnostic Writing Task</h2></div><p>This is <strong>formative</strong>. The rubric makes the baseline measurable so it can be compared with later writing.</p></div><div class="task"><h3>Write 120–150 Words</h3><p>Choose <strong>one</strong>: (1) an electrical/electronic <strong>device or system</strong>, (2) a laboratory <strong>method or process</strong>, or (3) one <strong>result</strong> from a project, experiment, simulation, or figure you understand.</p><div class="conditions"><strong>Baseline conditions:</strong> written <strong>in class</strong> · <strong>no AI tools</strong> · <strong>no dictionary</strong> · <strong>single draft</strong>. These conditions make later comparison meaningful.</div><p>Your paragraph should aim to be <strong class="key">formal</strong>, <strong class="key">objective</strong>, <strong class="key">precise</strong> and <strong class="key">clear</strong>. Use <strong>measurements, units or quantities</strong> where appropriate.</p><textarea placeholder="Write your diagnostic paragraph here..." style="min-height:180px"></textarea></div><div class="head" style="margin-top:24px"><div><span class="label">Baseline rubric</span><h2>Diagnostic Writing Rubric — 16 Points</h2></div><p>Complete the self-score first; the score can then be reviewed in class.</p></div><div class="table-scroll"><table class="rubric"><tr><th>Criterion</th><th>1</th><th>2</th><th>3</th><th>4</th></tr><tr><td><str